From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FatBoy721 <203330788+FatBoy721@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:05:32 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] nvme: apple: Keep post-M4 ANS live across suspend-to-idle

On the J714s (M5 Pro), closing the lid reset the machine. Aborting
pm_test=devices at each device in turn pinned the first reset on the
NVMe suspend: disabling the post-M4 ANS controller and rebuilding its
queues across system sleep takes the machine down.

For suspend-to-idle the controller does not need to go down at all:
user space is frozen and keep_link_powered() already holds its power
domains on. Return early there, before the controller is moved to
RESETTING. anv->suspended stays false, so resume returns early too.

Sleep through firmware (pm_suspend_via_firmware()) keeps the old path.
t6050_keep_live=0 restores it for suspend-to-idle as well.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
  drivers/nvme/host/apple.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
  1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/nvme/host/apple.c b/drivers/nvme/host/apple.c
index ef52797a0..c412facdd 100644
--- a/drivers/nvme/host/apple.c
+++ b/drivers/nvme/host/apple.c
@@ -38,6 +38,7 @@
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
 #include <linux/pm_domain.h>
 #include <linux/soc/apple/rtkit.h>
+#include <linux/suspend.h>
 #include <linux/soc/apple/sart.h>
 #include <linux/reset.h>
 #include <linux/time64.h>
@@ -2658,11 +2659,29 @@ static void apple_nvme_keep_link_powered(struct apple_nvme *anv)
 		device_set_awake_path(anv->pd_dev[i]);
 }
 
+/*
+ * On post-M4 ANS (needs_ioq_registers), disabling and rebuilding the controller
+ * across system sleep resets the machine (J714s, found by aborting
+ * pm_test=devices at each device in turn). For suspend-to-idle the controller
+ * can stay live: user space is frozen and keep_link_powered() holds its power
+ * domains on. Resume needs no change: anv->suspended stays false, so it
+ * returns early.
+ */
+static bool t6050_keep_live = true;
+module_param(t6050_keep_live, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(t6050_keep_live, "Keep post-M4 ANS NVMe live across suspend-to-idle (no controller disable/rebuild)");
+
 static int apple_nvme_suspend(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct apple_nvme *anv = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 	int ret;
 
+	if (anv->hw->needs_ioq_registers && READ_ONCE(t6050_keep_live) &&
+	    !pm_suspend_via_firmware()) {
+		apple_nvme_keep_link_powered(anv);
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	if (anv->hw->needs_ioq_registers) {
 		if (!nvme_change_ctrl_state(&anv->ctrl, NVME_CTRL_RESETTING))
 			return -EBUSY;
-- 
